  "step_3": "The decision reason prioritizes the maximum outcome when it differs, regardless of probability differences. Here, Lottery B has a higher maximum outcome (2500 vs. 2400), so the reason would prefer B. The individual’s justification reflects a similar logic: they acknowledge the 100 Euro disadvantage of A but reject it because the 1% probability advantage is not sufficient to compensate. This shows that the individual weighed the outcome difference (100 Euros) as decisive, aligning with the decision reason’s focus on maximum outcome. Although the individual also mentions probability, their final judgment is based on the outcome difference being too large to justify the small probability gain. Thus, the reasoning process matches the decision reason’s rule: the more favorable maximum outcome (B) is preferred. The individual did not use expected value or other probabilistic calculations, but instead relied on the relative importance of the outcome levels, which is the core of the given decision reason.",
